# UCE Sidekick — Cursor agent boundaries (uce repo)

**Desktop only.** Production edge + Lovable portal: **https://github.com/jeffatkins-filewisely/filewisely** — open that folder for Theo, `supabase/functions`, migrations, claim-batch / ack.

**Rule:** Edge/backend changes happen in **filewisely**. Desktop changes happen in **uce**. The `backend/` folder here is a mirror/reference, not production source of truth.

Stay in the lane the user requests.

## Default: server / edge lane (Lovable backend work)

**Allowed** (edit freely when task is edge, SQL, or contracts):

- `supabase/functions/**`
- `supabase/migrations/**`
- `supabase/_shared/**` (if present)
- `backend/contracts/**`
- `backend/supabase/**` (deploy reference / merge guides)
- `docs/contracts/**`
- `docs/CONTRACTS.md`, `docs/REPO_WORKFLOW.md`
- `scripts/**` (deploy, ops — not `scripts/build-release.ps1` unless release task)

**Forbidden** unless the user explicitly asks for desktop or portal UI:

- `src/pages/**`, `src/components/**`, `src/integrations/**` — Lovable portal; do not redesign
- `src-tauri/**` — Rust desktop agent (CCC sync, tray, capture pipeline)
- `src/main.js`, `src/*.js`, `index.html`, `vite.config.js` — embedded webview UI
- `.github/workflows/release.yml` — MSI/release pipeline
- `installer/**` — NSIS/printer setup
- `package.json` / `src-tauri/tauri.conf.json` version bumps — only for explicit Sidekick release tasks
- Auto-generated or design-system files the user did not name

## Desktop / Sidekick lane

When the user says Sidekick, desktop, Tauri, mirror writer, or CCC Import:

**Allowed:**

- `src-tauri/**`
- `src/**` (webview shell only)
- `docs/CCC_PACKAGE_SYNC.md`, `docs/DEVICE_HEALTH.md`, `docs/TRAY_SILENT_INSTALL.md`
- `docs/contracts/**`, `backend/contracts/**` (keep in sync with edge)
- `connection-doctor.html`, `src/connection-doctor.js`

**Forbidden:**

- `supabase/functions/**` — unless also syncing contracts both sides
- Portal `src/pages/**` / Lovable components

## Contracts

- Claim-batch request: `business_id`, `device_id`, `limit`
- Claim-batch response: `items[]` with mirror/cleanup job fields
- Ack request: `business_id`, `device_id`, `items[]` with `queue_id`, `source_table`, `source_id`, `status`, optional `written_path`
- See `docs/CONTRACTS.md` — update JSON Schema, Zod, and Rust together

## Git

- `git pull` before editing; `git push` after (user commits unless asked)
- Do not force-push `main`

## Prompt hygiene

- User should name exact paths: `supabase/functions/ccc-package-claim-batch/index.ts`
- If the diff touches files outside the requested lane, stop and narrow scope
